---
title: "sign_get_request (Legion Backend Authentication)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_extract_id: identifier = extract_unique_id(request)
    q_extract_id --> q_validate: identifier != null
    q_validate --> q_load_key: secret_key = load_signing_key()
    q_validate --> q_error: identifier == null
    q_error --> [*]: revert "missing identifier"
    q_load_key --> q_compute: signature = HMAC_SHA256(secret_key, identifier)
    q_compute --> q_attach: set_header("X-Signature", signature)
    q_attach --> [*]: return signed_request

    note right of q_extract_id
        INV-001: identifier is a unique value such as user_id or round_id
        INV-002: GET signing uses identifier string, not URL or query params
        INV-003: signing string differs from POST (body vs identifier) - mismatch causes auth failure
    end note
